# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R2; the
# spec-warden's `cfgone`, its second order).
#
# `fixedbugs-563-cap.h` defines `LIMIT` as 10 where nothing has, and
# `fixedbugs-563-limit.h` defines it as 100 whatever came before, which C11
# 6.10.3p2 forbids once the first has. Read in this order, `cap` would cap at
# 10 and every line after the second header read 100: until 2026-10-10 this
# built at exit 0 and printed 3 and 10, under a clang warning nobody read,
# where the other order of the two groups printed 3 and 50. It is refused
# now, told the other order's meaning and a header of the program's own that
# keeps this one, which the two `guess` fixes name.
extern "fixedbugs-563-cap.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function cap(v: i32) -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-563-limit.h"
    function half(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(half(x: 6))
    print(cap(v: 50))
